Based on domain knowledge of the warm forging process and the physical process flow described in Section  3.1 , a directed acyclic graph (DAG) was constructed as shown in Fig.  16 . The DAG encodes the following causal assumptions:  MHT, WS, and MFL are exogenous controllable variables with no common unmeasured causes among them. These are set by operators at the equipment level and are mutually independent in the experimental design. DT is causally influenced by MHT (higher billet temperature transfers more heat to the die) and by production continuity/time (thermal accumulation during continuous operation, as confirmed in Section  4.1 ). PT is causally influenced by MHT (directly, through billet temperature) and by DT (through heat transfer during die contact). The strong positive correlation between DT and PT ( \documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
